// workflows.jsonl — FULL workflow lane (run with --workflow, needs a running server).
// Each case drives the real plan → auto-approve ("proceed") → execute loop until the turn
// ends without a pause (completed) or the round cap is hit. Asserts run on the WHOLE run:
//   must_complete  — workflow finished (didn't stall awaiting input / hit max_rounds)
//   max_rounds     — total plan/approve/execute turns stayed bounded
//   min_steps      — the proposed plan had real decomposition
//   tools_include/any — tools the model actually executed across all rounds
// The workflow_outcome judge reads plan + executed tools + final response together.
// category defaults to "planning" (forces the planner/approval path). Keep prompts that
// the LOCAL model can finish; heavy multi-tool prompts are slow on local backends.
// MCP / cloud / Drive / web tool binding is NOT faithful in dry-run — use --workflow or --live
// (running server + network). Failures on ambiguous real-world prompts are intentional signals.
{"id": "wf_smoke", "prompt": "look up the current time, then tell me what time it will be 3 hours from now", "category": "planning", "expect": {"min_steps": 1, "max_rounds": 4, "must_complete": true, "tools_any": ["get_datetime", "get_time"]}, "judge": ["workflow_outcome"], "note": "cheap end-to-end proof of plan→approve→execute; side-effect free. workflow_outcome only — plan-quality is asserted on the richer cases."}
{"id": "wf_research_compare", "prompt": "research the 3 most popular python web frameworks and give me a short comparison", "category": "planning", "expect": {"min_steps": 1, "max_rounds": 5, "must_complete": true, "scout_before_plan": true, "gather_brief_present": true}, "judge": ["workflow_outcome"], "note": "single research+synthesize delegation = ONE delegate_to_research_agent step under subagent-first (the agent researches AND compares); outcome is the metric, not step granularity. wf_file_writeup covers the genuine 2-subagent gather-then-act case."}
{"id": "wf_file_writeup", "prompt": "research the top 3 note-taking apps and write a short comparison to a markdown file on my desktop", "category": "planning", "expect": {"min_steps": 2, "max_rounds": 6, "must_complete": true, "tools_any": ["write_file", "create_file", "propose_file_plan"]}, "judge": ["planner_quality", "workflow_outcome"], "note": "richer multi-step with a file-write side effect; verifies execution actually reaches a tool"}
{"id": "wf_screenshot_then_diagnose", "prompt": "take a screenshot of my desktop, then check if there are any system issues I should know about", "category": "planning", "expect": {"max_rounds": 5, "must_complete": true, "tools_include": ["capture_screen"]}, "budget": {"min_steps": 2}, "judge": ["workflow_outcome"], "note": "two independent, cheap, side-effect-free actions in one request; verifies the planner decomposes into 2 steps instead of collapsing to just one"}
{"id": "wf_reminder_then_confirm", "prompt": "set a reminder for me to review the budget tomorrow at 10am, then read it back to me to confirm", "category": "planning", "expect": {"min_steps": 2, "max_rounds": 5, "must_complete": true, "tools_any": ["set_reminder", "execute_future_task", "manage_cron"]}, "judge": ["workflow_outcome"], "note": "write-then-verify pattern: create a reminder and confirm it was stored, a common 2-step user flow"}
{"id": "wf_search_write_organize", "prompt": "look up 3 quick tips for staying focused while studying, save them to a text file, and put that file in a new folder called StudyTips", "category": "planning", "expect": {"min_steps": 3, "max_rounds": 7, "must_complete": true, "tools_any": ["write_file", "create_file"], "scout_before_plan": true}, "judge": ["planner_quality", "workflow_outcome"], "note": "genuine 3-step chain: research -> write -> organize/file-move; checks the planner doesn't drop the trailing organizational step"}
{"id": "wf_diagram_then_share", "prompt": "make a simple flowchart of a typical morning routine, then tell me it's ready to share with my roommate", "category": "planning", "expect": {"min_steps": 1, "max_rounds": 5, "must_complete": true, "tools_any": ["render_diagram", "load_skill"]}, "judge": ["workflow_outcome"], "note": "visual-generation workflow with a conversational confirmation tail; verifies the plan doesn't stall waiting on the 'share' half when no real send action was requested"}
{"id": "wf_calendar_then_reminder", "prompt": "check what's on my calendar for today, and if anything is in the afternoon set a reminder for 30 minutes before it", "category": "planning", "expect": {"min_steps": 2, "max_rounds": 6, "must_complete": true, "tools_any": ["google_calendar_check"]}, "judge": ["planner_quality", "workflow_outcome"], "note": "conditional multi-step: read calendar first, then a follow-up action gated on what was found; tests the plan handles a data-dependent second step"}
